apps/data_etl_app/src/data_etl_app/knowledge/prompts/final_texts/
!apps/data_etl_app/src/data_etl_app/knowledge/prompts/final_texts/
apps/data_etl_app/src/data_etl_app/knowledge/prompts/final_texts/*
!apps/data_etl_app/src/data_etl_app/knowledge/prompts/final_texts/static/
!apps/data_etl_app/src/data_etl_app/knowledge/prompts/final_texts/static/**
!apps/data_etl_app/src/data_etl_app/knowledge/prompts/skeletons/
!apps/data_etl_app/src/data_etl_app/knowledge/prompts/skeletons/*.txt
# Grounding evaluation instrument (apps/data_etl_app/tests/test_stages/grounding):
# the eval set, fixtures, per-run results/judgments, and ledger are deliberately
# persisted in git — they are the instrument's memory across runs.
!apps/data_etl_app/tests/test_stages/grounding/**/*.json
!apps/data_etl_app/tests/test_stages/grounding/**/*.jsonl
!apps/data_etl_app/tests/test_stages/grounding/**/*.txt
# Search-stage evaluation (apps/data_etl_app/tests/test_stages/search):
# the expectation set, per-run scorecards and the append-only metrics history
# are the instrument's memory across runs, so they must be tracked despite the
# blanket *.json / *.jsonl rules above. The per-run raw/ directories are the
# exception — they hold pulled request bodies with the scraped SITE TEXT and
# stay ignored (each also carries its own .gitignore).
!apps/data_etl_app/tests/test_stages/search/**/*.json
!apps/data_etl_app/tests/test_stages/search/**/*.jsonl
!apps/data_etl_app/tests/test_stages/search/**/*.txt
# Synthesis-stage evaluation (apps/data_etl_app/tests/test_stages/synthesis):
# same rationale — the expectation set, per-run scorecards/work orders/verdicts
# and the cumulative judgment ledger are the instrument's memory across runs.
# evidence_snapshots/ is the exception (pulled wire payloads hold the scraped
# SITE TEXT) and stays ignored via the folder's own .gitignore.
!apps/data_etl_app/tests/test_stages/synthesis/**/*.json
!apps/data_etl_app/tests/test_stages/synthesis/**/*.jsonl
!apps/data_etl_app/tests/test_stages/synthesis/**/*.txt
# Mention-stage evaluation (apps/data_etl_app/tests/test_stages/mention_collection):
# same rationale. Its GOLDEN CORPUS (goldens/) is the instrument's ground truth,
# derived from the pinned texts rather than from any run, so it is tracked like
# the sibling eval sets. Per-run data under history/ stays ignored by the
# blanket rules below; the golden labels quote the site text but never carry it
# wholesale, which is what keeps them committable.
!apps/data_etl_app/tests/test_stages/mention_collection/**/*.json
!apps/data_etl_app/tests/test_stages/mention_collection/**/*.jsonl
!apps/data_etl_app/tests/test_stages/mention_collection/**/*.txt

# --- Stage-evaluation RUN DATA stays off GitHub (2026-08-27, user decision) ---
# The per-stage blocks above re-include *.json/*.jsonl/*.txt so each stage's
# INSTRUMENT is tracked — eval sets, config, harness code, docs, tests. Its
# per-run evidence is a different animal: golden-corpus scale (search history
# 4.8M, synthesis history 4.0M + evidence_snapshots 5.0M) and partly verbatim
# scraped SITE TEXT pulled from Mongo. None of it belongs in the repo.
#
# Written as `<dir>/**` rather than `<dir>/` on purpose: ignoring the directory
# itself would stop git descending into it, and the negations below would then
# be unreachable.
apps/data_etl_app/tests/test_stages/*/history/**
apps/data_etl_app/tests/test_stages/*/results/**
apps/data_etl_app/tests/test_stages/*/evidence_snapshots/**
apps/data_etl_app/tests/test_stages/*/**/raw/**

# ...with ONE exception per stage: the small cross-run trend file. These are
# tens of KB, contain no site text, and are the entire point of a longitudinal
# instrument — without them a fresh clone cannot compare today's run to any
# previous one. Delete these lines if even they should stay local.
!apps/data_etl_app/tests/test_stages/*/history/metrics.jsonl
!apps/data_etl_app/tests/test_stages/*/history/ledger.json
!apps/data_etl_app/tests/test_stages/*/history/LEDGER.md
!apps/data_etl_app/tests/test_stages/*/history/metrics_scoreboard.csv

# ...and the per-run WRITTEN ANALYSIS. FINDINGS/SUMMARY/JUDGED/notes are prose
# in the KBs with no site text in them, and they are what the run data was
# gathered to produce — losing them from the repo would leave the conclusions
# living only on one laptop. Re-including needs the two directory lines first:
# git cannot re-include a file whose parent directory is excluded.
!apps/data_etl_app/tests/test_stages/*/history/runs/
!apps/data_etl_app/tests/test_stages/*/history/runs/*/
!apps/data_etl_app/tests/test_stages/*/history/runs/*/*.md
# analyses one level deeper (e.g. a run's table_ab/ experiment notes) are
# tracked the same way; their data files stay ignored
!apps/data_etl_app/tests/test_stages/*/history/runs/*/*/
!apps/data_etl_app/tests/test_stages/*/history/runs/*/*/*.md

# The sample scraped-text corpus: 4.7M of verbatim site text (acimachine.com
# alone is 3.9M). It was untracked but NOT ignored, so any `git add -A` would
# have committed the whole corpus. Same class of data as the run evidence.
apps/data_etl_app/src/data_etl_app/knowledge/sample_scraped_texts/
# same class: the markdown_v2 reseeded corpus (14M of scraped site text) and
# the 24M scraper output-format sample — pinned locally, never in git
apps/data_etl_app/tests/test_stages/sample_scraped_markdowns/
pipeline_v3_evidence/2026-08-28_scraper_output_format_sample/*
# ...but the machinery in it is re-runnable instrument, not data
!pipeline_v3_evidence/2026-08-28_scraper_output_format_sample/*.py
!pipeline_v3_evidence/2026-08-28_scraper_output_format_sample/README.md
